  "description": "Filter golden of phase3.2_proc-filter-families (held-out): levels cases on the authored Tier 2b bevelled cube low mesh with its knob, texture set 2048 px, L32F User channels. Every User channel is a fill of the authored content-grey bitmap (UV projection, tiled 8 x 8, Nearest, so one bitmap texel per texel); User0 is that content alone, and each case adds one content effect on its own channel, the starter-asset filter found by the documented search s:starterassets u:filter n:<name>= with the case's parameters, or the native levels effect: User1 defaults: the native levels effect (defaults); User2 recipe-bracer-r: the native levels effect (input_min = 0.42, input_max = 0.6, gamma = 1.0, output_min = 0.0, output_max = 1.0, clamp = 0); User3 interior-a: the native levels effect (input_min = 0.1, input_max = 0.85, gamma = 1.7, output_min = 0.05, output_max = 0.9, clamp = 0); User4 interior-b: the native levels effect (input_min = 0.3, input_max = 0.55, gamma = 0.4, output_min = 0.2, output_max = 0.95, clamp = 1). Painter then bakes World Space Normals low as high (OutputSize 11, LowAsHigh, DilationWidth 0, every other baking parameter at Painter's default) to mark its UV coverage. The User maps and the World Space Normals map are exported as OpenEXR 32f, padding passthrough, no dithering; recorded twice (same session; after save and reopen). Bake backend uncontrolled.",
